              "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
              "markdown": "![Understanding the Four Cs of Diamonds: Your Guide to Quality ...](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/09242103-2330-0066-0000-298fe0f743f3:4)\nThe 4Cs of diamonds are [Cut](https://www.americangemsociety.org/4cs-of-diamonds/), Color, Clarity , and [Carat Weight](https://4cs.gia.edu/en-us/4cs-of-diamond-quality/) , which serve as the universal standard established by the Gemological Institute of America (GIA) to evaluate and grade diamond quality.[[1]](https://4cs.gia.edu/en-us/4cs-of-diamond-quality/)[[2]](https://www.brilliantearth.com/guides/4-cs-of-diamonds/)\n\n### Cut\n\n- **What it means:** How well a diamond's facets interact with light. It is widely considered the most important factor for sparkle.[[1]](https://www.americangemsociety.org/4cs-of-diamonds/)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/M21gEZX6n6Q)[[3]](https://www.gabrielny.com/blog/the-4-cs-of-diamonds/)\n- **Grades:** Ranging from Excellent to Poor. A precise cut creates brilliance, fire, and scintillation.[[1]](https://www.brilliantearth.com/guides/4-cs-of-diamonds/)[[2]](https://www.grownbrilliance.com/education-guide/learn-about-the-4cs)\n\n### Color\n\n- **What it means:** The absence of color in a diamond. Truly colorless stones are the rarest and most valuable.[[1]](https://www.gabrielny.com/blog/the-4-cs-of-diamonds/)[[2]](https://www.helzberg.com/jewelry-advice/the-4cs-of-diamonds.html)\n- **Grades:** Scored on a scale from **D** (completely colorless) to **Z** (light yellow or brown tint).[[1]](https://www.helzberg.com/jewelry-advice/the-4cs-of-diamonds.html)[[2]](https://www.brilliantearth.com/guides/4-cs-of-diamonds/)\n\n### Clarity\n\n- **What it means:** The presence of internal imperfections (inclusions) or external flaws (blemishes).[[1]](https://www.americangemsociety.org/4cs-of-diamonds/)\n- **Grades:** Ranging from **FL** (Flawless) down to **I3** (Included). Most buyers look for \"eye-clean\" stones where flaws are invisible without magnification.[[1]](https://www.vrai.com/journal/post/diamonds-defined-the-ultimate-4cs-guide)[[2]](https://www.brilliantearth.com/guides/4-cs-of-diamonds/)[[3]](https://www.gabrielny.com/blog/the-4-cs-of-diamonds/)\n\n### Carat\n\n- **What it means:** The weight measurement of the diamond. One carat equals 0.2 grams.[[1]](https://ecksand.com/blogs/stories/what-are-the-4-cs-of-diamonds)[[2]](https://www.brilliantearth.com/guides/4-cs-of-diamonds/)\n- **Note:** Carat measures weight, not physical size, which can vary based on the diamond's shape and cut depth.[[1]](https://www.kay.com/4cs-of-diamonds)\n\nIf you are shopping for a piece, let me know your **target budget** or **preferred diamond shape** , and I can help you decide which of the 4Cs to prioritize.",
